hxg4 27. Rh2 Bd5 28. h5 {The obvious move of 28.Rf2, was the
coupe juste and would have left the advantage with White. }
Rxf4 29. Bxf4 Bxf4 30. Ne4 Be3+ 31. Kg2 Rf8 32. Rf1 Rf5
33. Rhh1 {Here, again, we are at a loss to understand how
White could be guilty of such a glaring mistake. Had he played
instead, 33.Rh4, the game must have been won without any
trouble.} Re5 34. Kg3 Bxe4 35. Bxe4 Rxe4 36. Rh4 e5 37. Rxg4
